      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-226013",
      ":question/problem": "Consider a normal population with unknown mean and standard deviation $\u03c3 = 2$. Find the smallest sample size $n$ required to ensure that the margin of error for the $95%$ confidence interval for the population mean is at most $0.06$.\n\n*Hint: Use the fact that $P(Z > 1.96) = 0.025$, where $Z\u223cN(0, 1)$.*\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
