      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-251191",
      ":question/problem": "Consider a population with unknown mean and standard deviation $\u03c3 = 8$. Find the smallest sample size $n$ required to ensure that the margin of error for the $80%$ confidence interval for the population mean is at most $1$.\n\n*Hint: Given a random variable $Z\u223cN(0, 1)$, the table below shows the $z$-scores $z_{p}$ such that $P(Z > z_{p}) = p$ for some particular values of $p$.*\n\n| $p$ | $0.100$ | $0.050$ | $0.025$ | $0.010$ | $0.005$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $z_{p}$ | $1.282$ | $1.645$ | $1.960$ | $2.326$ | $2.576$ |\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
    }
